  "summary": "Postinstall dependency script fetches and executes remote installer via curl | sh",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js runs execSync(\"curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh |...\") from a package lifecycle path, fetching an unpinned shell script from a mutable GitHub branch and piping it through a shell interpreter on the installer's machine. The same script imports child_process, https, fs, and os, reads os.homedir() and process.platform, and issues additional network requests to https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com. bin/awk.js and scripts/model-manager.js contain further child_process + http/https request primitives. Because the install-time payload is fetched from a mutable branch head over the network and executed without any hash or signature check, whoever controls that branch controls what runs on every install.",
